## Rotating Card – Hover‑to‑Flip Example

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a card with a front and a back side.  
When you hover over the card it flips (rotates) around the Y‑axis.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card on Hover</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Container (perspective) ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;          /* card width */
  height: 200px;         /* card height */
  perspective: 1000px;   /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
  margin: 50px auto;     /* center horizontally */
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  Card (3D transform) ---------- */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
  transition: transform 0.6s;     /* smooth flip */
}

/* Hover state – flip the card */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide the back side when facing away */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #fff;
}

/* Front face */
.card-front {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4e54c8, #8f94fb);
}

/* Back face – rotated 180° so it starts hidden */
.card-back {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff416c, #ff4b2b);
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-face card-front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="card-face card-back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1. `perspective`** | The wrapper gives the 3D space. | Without it the rotation would look flat. |
| **2. `transform-style: preserve-3d`** | Keeps child elements in 3D. | Needed for the backface visibility to work. |
| **3. `backface-visibility: hidden`** | Hides the side that is turned away. | Prevents the backside from showing through. |
| **4. `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on hover** | Flips the card. | The transition makes it smooth. |
| **5. `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on the back face** | Positions the back side opposite the front. | So when the card flips, the back becomes visible. |

### Customisation tips

| Property | What to change | Example |
|----------|----------------|---------|
| `width / height` | Card size | `width: 400px; height: 250px;` |
| `perspective` | Depth of the flip | `perspective: 800px;` |
| `transition` | Speed / easing | `transition: transform 0.8s cubic-bezier(.4,0,.2,1);` |
| `background` | Colours / gradients | `background: #333;` |
| `font-size` | Text size | `font-size: 1.5rem;` |

Feel free to replace the text inside `.card-front` and `.card-back` with images, icons, or any other content you like. Happy coding!
